<title>UK: Copper steadier on LME, July borrowing increases.</title>
<headline>Copper steadier on LME, July borrowing increases.</headline>
<text>
<p>COPPER - Around highs, as increased borrowing of July dates underpins backwardations. July/one day trades at $13, July/week at $47.</p>
<p>LEAD - Drifts back under $660.</p>
<p>ZINC - Quiet and slightly lower. Sept/threes trades at $12 backwardation.</p>
<p>ALUMINIUM - Softer, not helped by 6,900-tonne stock rise.</p>
<p>TIN - Quietly steady. NICKEL - Slightly steadier.</p>
</text>
